    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class (the other two are support base classes), so the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipTier` field following the codebase's existing convention for computed read-only owner attributes (`displayName`, `initials`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipTier` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (next to `membershipNumber`), so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient` computed getter `getMembershipTier()` alongside `getDisplayName()`:\n   ```java\n   boolean uniquelyNamed = Integer.valueOf(0).equals(this.namesakeCount);\n   boolean hasEmail = this.email != null && !this.email.isEmpty();\n   return uniquelyNamed && hasEmail ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   ```\n\nThe tier derives purely from the owner's own state (`namesakeCount` + `email`), so it belongs on the model as a single-responsibility computed property \u2014 exactly mirroring `getDisplayName`/`getInitials`. MapStruct maps it into the DTO by name automatically, no mapper changes needed. Null-safe: a null `namesakeCount` correctly yields `BRONZE`.\n\nAll tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS), including both new cases: SILVER for a unique owner with an email, BRONZE when no email is present.",
